    {
      "id": "6aAS5shV-VGG0LkYqyIb7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5085.742808690153,
      "y": 4979.628257624688,
      "width": 651.1194458007812,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1535004312,
      "version": 241,
      "versionNonce": 1858128360,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791558050806,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "One call for all 200 questions is what makes the 90-second limit\neasy. A per-question loop with reloads would risk it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "One call for all 200 questions is what makes the 90-second limit easy. A per-question loop with reloads would risk it.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aDQZy5eSNzmiToMnWqRK6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5090.935384780645,
      "y": 4801.159426244477,
      "width": 640.87939453125,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 686341016,
      "version": 196,
      "versionNonce": 1912023192,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791558050806,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "You pass the token batch, your metadata list as the corpus for\nthis call, and k. bm25s scores every question, takes the top k\nper question, and looks each winning position up in the corpus\nyou passed. Because the metadata is passed explicitly, you get\ndicts with file path and character range back, not text.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "You pass the token batch, your metadata list as the corpus for this call, and k. bm25s scores every question, takes the top k per question, and looks each winning position up in the corpus you passed. Because the metadata is passed explicitly, you get dicts with file path and character range back, not text.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3WAKaPsXJ8gZK0T-AYbSP",
