    {
      "id": "vvoIj8jGXWEhhc9I1brTl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7889.164419879668,
      "y": 5076.767772468947,
      "width": 489.12535108334816,
      "height": 479.81243133544905,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2051932641,
      "version": 165,
      "versionNonce": 436417437,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791890146555,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "decides what to compute. It\nknows the structure of the\nmetric: it checks that the\nstudent file is valid, pairs\nquestions by question_id, cuts\neach retrieved list to its first\nk, and averages the per-\nquestion recalls into one\nnumber per k. It never decides\non its own whether two\nsources overlap. It asks the\nmatcher.",
      "fontSize": 31.987495422363267,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "decides what to compute. It knows the structure of the metric: it checks that the student file is valid, pairs questions by question_id, cuts each retrieved list to its first k, and averages the per-question recalls into one number per k. It never decides on its own whether two sources overlap. It asks the matcher.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LWi0vNpOD1RcD3f-z8ht8",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 7832.81510435157,
      "y": 5023.8927877277365,
      "width": 585.9843444824219,
      "height": 566.4375305175781,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
