      "originalText": "#Methods",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "SbyJNEAq688Idbq8rZOb6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7761.785010894427,
      "y": 6947.039716597975,
      "width": 544.385009765625,
      "height": 280,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1830324424,
      "version": 348,
      "versionNonce": 164660707,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791796544831,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette: a problem if any question has more than\n max(k_values) sources, or a source longer than max_context_length.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-pair_questions(student, lookup) -> (pairs, skipped, unanswered):\n one pass, O(1) lookups, collects both unmatched sides.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over evaluated questions.\n A k above the stored k only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette: a problem if any question has more than\n max(k_values) sources, or a source longer than max_context_length.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-pair_questions(student, lookup) -> (pairs, skipped, unanswered):\n one pass, O(1) lookups, collects both unmatched sides.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over evaluated questions.\n A k above the stored k only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
