      "index": "b9y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1627339160,
      "version": 168,
      "versionNonce": 146623535,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791639008805,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette, with k = max(k_values). Problems:\n student.k above k, a question with more than k sources,\n a source longer than max_context_length. The stored k is not\n compared to the real count: the moulinette accepts that.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-pair_questions(student, lookup) -> (pairs, unknown_ids):\n student id absent from truth: clean error (moulinette: KeyError).\n truth id with no student result: recall 0, still evaluated.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over ALL truth questions.\n A k above the retrieved count only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette, with k = max(k_values). Problems:\n student.k above k, a question with more than k sources,\n a source longer than max_context_length. The stored k is not\n compared to the real count: the moulinette accepts that.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-pair_questions(student, lookup) -> (pairs, unknown_ids):\n student id absent from truth: clean error (moulinette: KeyError).\n truth id with no student result: recall 0, still evaluated.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over ALL truth questions.\n A k above the retrieved count only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "P4s8fVY5eD9EWOLs1yhx4",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 7709.318115173834,
      "y": 6503.164975544382,
      "width": 1467.9379272460933,
      "height": 1373.9997863769531,
