    {
      "id": "e9BGNOgpGFvDsR9nZcgR5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8549.65088323333,
      "y": 5294.593150435483,
      "width": 544.385009765625,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 520837016,
      "version": 412,
      "versionNonce": 503386511,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791958756616,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette: a problem if any question has more than\n max(k_values) sources, or a source longer than max_context_length.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over evaluated questions.\n A k above the stored k only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-build_truth_lookup(truth) -> Dict[str, List[MinimalSource]]:\n one dict question_id -> truth sources. Fails on duplicate ids.\n-validate_student(student) -> List[str]:\n mimics the moulinette: a problem if any question has more than\n max(k_values) sources, or a source longer than max_context_length.\n Empty list = valid. No recall is computed when invalid.\n-question_recall(truth_sources, retrieved, k) -> float:\n slice retrieved to its first k, then found sources / total sources.\n Defines the zero-truth-sources case.\n-evaluate(student, truth) -> EvaluationReport:\n validate, pair, then mean recall per k over evaluated questions.\n A k above the stored k only warns: recall is still computed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
